# Task 3: Teacher Course Management Implementation Plan

As Principal Full-Stack Developer, this plan outlines the architecture, database integration, and UI design for **Teacher Course Management**, covering the `/teacher/dashboard`, `/teacher/courses/create`, and the dynamic `/teacher/courses/[courseId]/builder` curriculum editor.

---

## Architecture & Data Flow

```mermaid
graph TD
    TeacherDashboard["/teacher/dashboard<br>(Instructor Studio Table)"]
    CreateCoursePage["/teacher/courses/create<br>(Course Metadata Form)"]
    CourseBuilderPage["/teacher/courses/[courseId]/builder<br>(Dynamic Curriculum Editor)"]
    
    ServerActions["Server Actions (actions/courses.ts)"]
    SupabaseDB["Supabase PostgreSQL<br>(courses, modules, lessons)"]

    TeacherDashboard -->|"Click 'Create Course'"| CreateCoursePage
    CreateCoursePage -->|"Submit createCourseAction()"| ServerActions
    ServerActions -->|"Insert into courses"| SupabaseDB
    ServerActions -->|"Redirect"| CourseBuilderPage
    
    CourseBuilderPage -->|"createModuleAction()"| ServerActions
    CourseBuilderPage -->|"createLessonAction()"| ServerActions
    CourseBuilderPage -->|"reorderCurriculumAction()"| ServerActions
    CourseBuilderPage -->|"publishCourseAction()"| ServerActions
    
    CourseBuilderPage -->|"Back to studio"| TeacherDashboard
```

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Route Structure**:
> - Dashboard: `/teacher/dashboard` (with full course table, stats, and action triggers).
> - Course Creation: `/teacher/courses/create` (creates course record and redirects straight into the curriculum builder).
> - Curriculum Builder: `/teacher/courses/[courseId]/builder` (visual module and lesson tree editor).
>
> **Interactive Reordering Pattern**:
> To guarantee flawless React 19 / Next.js 15 compatibility and mobile friendliness without heavy third-party drag bundles, we will implement an accessible, fluid reordering system with intuitive **Move Up / Move Down** controls, inline drag indicators, and instant visual state updates synced to PostgreSQL `order_index`.

